# Build context exclusions for `docker build .` at the repo root.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY --link . .` then `pnpm install`. Anything left in
# here is shipped into the image, so host-side installs and build output must
# be excluded: a host node_modules makes pnpm try to purge and reinstall the
# modules dir, which prompts interactively and hangs the build (no TTY).

# Dependencies — regenerated inside the image by `pnpm install`
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store/

# VCS / CI metadata.
# NOTE: .husky must NOT be excluded — the root `prepare` script runs
# `node .husky/install.mjs`, so pnpm install fails outright if it is missing.
# The script self-skips when CI=true or NODE_ENV=production.
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Build output — regenerated inside the image by `pnpm -r run build`
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/out
.out/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ...except this one, which is committed to git and not regenerated by a build
!packages/db-data-prisma/dist
!packages/db-data-prisma/dist/**

# Caches
.cache
.swc/
**/.eslintcache
.claude-flow

# Local env files (secrets). Tracked .env / .env.development / .env.test are
# required by the build and are deliberately NOT excluded.
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/.netrc
*.pem

# Editor / OS
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# Logs & test output
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
/coverage

# Docker's own files
.dockerignore
